+## Correction trial
+
+2026-10-02. Before-state: commit `c92fe28`.
+
+Supplied correction, verbatim:
+
+> An agreement may cover several services. An organisation’s participant role may differ for each service covered by that agreement.
+
+The corrected model introduces coverage as a conceptual association. Under the
+retained single-organisation assumption, its agreement determines the organisation
+whose service-specific role facts it carries. This representation is provisional;
+the supplied correction settles multiple service support and role scope only.
+The initial one-service assumption and agreement-only role scope are superseded.
+
+Additional guidance read: none; reused the initial readings. Read the three
+existing model, glossary and scenario documents (approximately 1,050 words).
+Manually traced unchanged ordinary and identity examples, multiple coverage,
+distinct agreement results, different roles across services, and a shared service
+across agreements without role leakage. Preserved unresolved multiple participants,
+simultaneous roles, missing coverage and missing role meanings. Checked all 12
+local links and `git diff --check`; both passed. Reconciled ER multiplicities with
+the retained assumptions and new requirement. Renderer remains unavailable as
+recorded above; no parse or visual verification, network or runtime work occurred.
+No new material guidance friction was encountered. The role representation needs
+an explicit explanation of its dependence on A1 so readers do not generalize it
+to multiple participants.
